# Purpose and audience: executable specification evidence for the owning engineering team.
# @req REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
# research: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; design: doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md

"""
## Purpose and audience

Purpose: pin that a `.?` existence check in VALUE position on the left of
`and`/`or` short-circuits correctly on the seed Cranelift JIT lane — an absent
`.?` must not evaluate the right-hand side, and the expression must yield the
same bool as the interpreter lane — and that `simple lint` of a warning-free
target therefore completes cleanly on the forced-JIT lane with a verdict
byte-identical to the interpreter lane.
Audience: compiler engineers maintaining the seed HIR/MIR lowering and the
lint JIT-parity lane.

Bug: doc/08_tracking/bug/lint_forced_jit_clean_target_unwrap_none_2026-11-27.md
— with the lint entry closure truly on the JIT lane, linting a warning-free
target on the forced-JIT lane crashed fail-closed:
`error: called unwrap on None` (rc 127, ~18 s, any clean .spl). Root cause
(SEED HIR lowering, NOT lint logic): `and`/`or` return a bool and decide on
operand presence, and `x.?` in condition position (`if x.?:`) is lowered to
the `rt_is_present` bool predicate — but the same `x.?` in VALUE position
(`val c = x.? and x.unwrap() == ...`) was lowered to the raw `T?` word whose
absent arm is the canonical nil sentinel `3` (non-zero). The MIR short-circuit
branch tests that word with `!= 0`, so an absent `x.?` read as TRUTHY on the
JIT lane: the RHS ran regardless, and `config.profile.unwrap()` (lint
`_LintMain/entry_and_fixes.spl`, profile legitimately None for the resolved
config) crashed. The interpreter's `BinOp::And` always returns
`Value::Bool` with `.?` special-cased as a presence test, so only the JIT lane
diverged. Fix: `hir/lower/expr/operators.rs lower_binary` now coerces
`.?` operands to the same bool presence predicate condition position gets
(`coerce_exists_value_to_bool_in_place`), mirroring the pre-existing
`not x.?` fix in `lower_unary`.

## Operator workflow (re-verification recipe)

The test runner refuses a SIMPLE_BINARY that differs from the binary running
the spec, so each run below uses the binary under test as both runner and
child. Isolation knobs used throughout:
`SIMPLE_HIR_CACHE_DIR=$PWD/build/p3cache/lintunwrap/hir-cache` and
`TMPDIR=$PWD/build/p3cache/lintunwrap/tmp`.

1. RED: build the pre-fix seed (any commit before the `lower_binary`
   coercion) and run it against itself:
     cd src/compiler_rust && \
       CC="$HOME/.simple/toolchains/llvm-mingw-20260922-ucrt-x86_64/bin/clang.exe" \
       CARGO_TARGET_DIR=C:/dev/lanes/p3-sweep/build/p3cache/lintunwrap/cargo-target \
       cargo build --release -p simple-driver
     SIMPLE_LIB=src SIMPLE_BINARY=$PWD/build/p3cache/lintunwrap/cargo-target/release/simple.exe \
       build/p3cache/lintunwrap/cargo-target/release/simple.exe test \
       test/01_unit/compiler/seed_jit_value_position_dotq_short_circuit_spec.spl
   Both examples FAIL: the probe child on the JIT lane evaluates the
   `and`-RHS (`A-RHS=1`, `A-RES=true`) and then dies with
   `error: called unwrap on None` (rc 127) at the unwrap crash shape; the
   lint child dies the same way before printing any verdict. Pre-fix
   evidence on the fixing lane: build/p3cache/lintunwrap/logs/repro-jit-stderr.log
   (rc 127) vs build/p3cache/lintunwrap/logs/repro-interp-stdout.log (rc 0,
   `Lint passed: all files clean`).
2. GREEN: current tree (the `lower_binary` coercion), same build + test
   command. Both examples pass; the two lanes' lint stdout is byte-identical
   after removing the `[engine-receipt]` line the JIT child is asked to print.
3. Direct probe without the spec:
     SIMPLE_LIB=src SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit \
       build/p3cache/lintunwrap/cargo-target/release/simple.exe run \
       build/p3cache/lintunwrap/dotq_probe.spl
   (the spec writes its own copies under
   build/p3cache/lintunwrap/spec/<pid>_<micros>/ — the lane-isolated scratch
   namespace, NOT build/test/, which concurrent lanes' suites sweep; any copy
   of the embedded probe source works). Expect the exact marker block
   documented in the example, rc 0. With `SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter`
   the stdout is byte-identical.

## Compatibility and limitations

Each example shells out to the seed binary (`SIMPLE_BIN` / `SIMPLE_BINARY` /
`SIMPLE_RUNTIME` / `SIMPLE_TEST_BINARY`, default `bin/simple`) through
`sh -c` with a shell env prefix: the test runner's child-env scrub
(`SIMPLE_TEST_CHILD_ENV_SCRUB=1`, test_runner_mode_env_leak_2026_11_12) strips
`SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE` pins from direct `process_run` spawns, and the shell
prefix is that scrub's documented escape hatch (same pattern as
test/01_unit/compiler/seed_lint_entry_stays_on_jit_lane_spec.spl).
`SIMPLE_ENGINE_RECEIPT=1` travels in the same prefix for the JIT children;
the receipt is the non-forgeable lane oracle (`engine=cranelift-jit
demoted=no`). Each JIT lint child compiles the whole lint closure and takes
~40 s wall. The lint target is a synthetic warning-free probe
(`fn main(): print "ok"`), written under build/p3cache/lintunwrap/spec/ —
the closure under test
is the lint command itself, exercised through the same
`_append_semantic_api_results` site that crashed.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.spec.step
use std.io_runtime.{process_run_timeout, env_get, file_write, file_exists, dir_create_all,
    getpid, time_now_unix_micros}

fn simple_binary() -> text:
    var configured = env_get("SIMPLE_BIN") ?? ""
    if configured == "":
        configured = env_get("SIMPLE_BINARY") ?? ""
    if configured == "":
        configured = env_get("SIMPLE_RUNTIME") ?? ""
    if configured == "":
        configured = env_get("SIMPLE_TEST_BINARY") ?? ""
    if configured.len() > 0:
        return configured
    "bin/simple"

fn probe_dir() -> text:
    # Lane-isolated scratch: NOT build/test/ — other lanes' spec suites sweep
    # build/test/ concurrently (observed 2026-11-28: a parallel suite removed
    # this spec's freshly-written probe between write and child spawn, and the
    # child failed with a spurious `semantic: variable rhs_ran not found`).
    "build/p3cache/lintunwrap/spec/{getpid()}_{time_now_unix_micros()}"

fn write_probe_file(name: text, source: text) -> text:
    dir_create_all(probe_dir())
    val path = probe_dir() + "/" + name
    val wrote = file_write(path, source)
    if not file_exists(path):
        print "file_write failed for {path}: {wrote}"
        expect(false).to_equal(true)
    path

# Behavioral probe for the value-position `.?` short-circuit defect: an absent
# `.?` on the LHS of `and` must not evaluate the RHS (interpreter semantics,
# which `and` must mirror on every lane). The C- shape is the exact lint crash
# reduction (`x.? and x.unwrap()`); the O-/P- shapes prove the `or` and
# present-arm paths still evaluate the RHS exactly as the interpreter does.
# No globals and no string interpolation in the probe source: the marker
# count/placement IS the RHS-evaluation evidence (a global counter made the
# probe sensitive to module-global resolution under SIMPLE_LIB=src, and brace
# interpolation in spec string literals is resolved by a concurrently
# refactored frontend — 2026-11-28).
fn write_dotq_probe() -> text:
    write_probe_file("dotq_probe.spl",
        "fn side_effect() -> bool:\n" +
        "    print(\"RHS-RAN\")\n" +
        "    true\n" +
        "\n" +
        "fn main() -> i64:\n" +
        "    val absent: text? = nil\n" +
        "    val present: text? = Some(\"p\")\n" +
        "    val a = absent.? and side_effect()\n" +
        "    if a:\n" +
        "        print(\"A-RES=true\")\n" +
        "    else:\n" +
        "        print(\"A-RES=false\")\n" +
        "    val c = absent.? and absent.unwrap() == \"x\"\n" +
        "    if c:\n" +
        "        print(\"C-RES=true\")\n" +
        "    else:\n" +
        "        print(\"C-RES=false\")\n" +
        "    val o = absent.? or side_effect()\n" +
        "    if o:\n" +
        "        print(\"O-RES=true\")\n" +
        "    else:\n" +
        "        print(\"O-RES=false\")\n" +
        "    val p = present.? and side_effect()\n" +
        "    if p:\n" +
        "        print(\"P-RES=true\")\n" +
        "    else:\n" +
        "        print(\"P-RES=false\")\n" +
        "    0\n")

# Warning-free lint target: the acceptance shape of
# lint_forced_jit_clean_target_unwrap_none_2026-11-27 (verified warning-free
# under the repository lint config on the interpreter lane).
fn write_clean_lint_target() -> text:
    write_probe_file("clean_probe.spl", "fn main():\n    print \"ok\"\n")

fn run_sh_child(script: text) -> (text, text, i64):
    # 15 min per child: a forced-JIT lint child compiles the whole lint
    # closure (~40 s warm cache, minutes cold) and the interpreter-lane child
    # takes ~3-10 min under build-farm load; the sibling lane contract spec
    # (seed_lint_entry_stays_on_jit_lane_spec.spl) uses an unbounded
    # process_run for the same reason.
    process_run_timeout("sh", ["-c", script], 900000)

fn receipt_line(combined: text) -> text:
    for raw in combined.split("\n"):
        val line = raw.trim()
        if line.contains("[engine-receipt]"):
            return line
    ""

fn receipt_field(line: text, key: text) -> text:
    val marker = key + "="
    val start = line.index_of(marker)
    if start < 0:
        return ""
    val rest = line.substring(start + marker.len(), line.len())
    val stop = rest.index_of(" ")
    if stop < 0:
        return rest
    rest.substring(0, stop)

describe "value-position .? short-circuits on the seed JIT lane":
    # @manual scenario evidence

    it "an absent .? LHS does not evaluate the and-RHS, identically on both lanes":
        step("Write the behavioral probe and run it on the forced JIT lane and the interpreter lane")
        val probe = write_dotq_probe()
        val bin = simple_binary()
        val (jit_out, jit_err, jit_code) = run_sh_child(
            "SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit \"{bin}\" run \"{probe}\"")
        val (interp_out, _, interp_code) = run_sh_child(
            "SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter \"{bin}\" run \"{probe}\"")
        step("Both lanes exit 0 and agree byte-for-byte")
        expect(jit_code).to_equal(0)
        expect(interp_code).to_equal(0)
        expect(jit_out == interp_out).to_equal(true)
        step("The absent arm never ran the RHS; or/present arms ran it once each (RHS-RAN markers)")
        val expected = "A-RES=false\nC-RES=false\nRHS-RAN\nO-RES=true\nRHS-RAN\nP-RES=true"
        expect(jit_out.contains(expected)).to_equal(true)
        if not jit_out.contains(expected):
            print "probe stdout:\n{jit_out}\nstderr:\n{jit_err}"

    it "lint of a warning-free target is clean on the forced JIT lane, byte-identical to the interpreter lane":
        step("Write the warning-free target and lint it on the forced JIT lane")
        val target = write_clean_lint_target()
        val bin = simple_binary()
        val (jit_out, jit_err, jit_code) = run_sh_child(
            "SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit SIMPLE_ENGINE_RECEIPT=1 \"{bin}\" lint \"{target}\"")
        step("The JIT child receipts the compiled engine with no demotion and lints clean")
        expect(jit_code).to_equal(0)
        val line = receipt_line(jit_out + jit_err)
        expect(line == "").to_equal(false)
        expect(receipt_field(line, "engine")).to_equal("cranelift-jit")
        expect(receipt_field(line, "demoted")).to_equal("no")
        step("Lint the same target on the interpreter lane")
        val (interp_out, _, interp_code) = run_sh_child(
            "SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter \"{bin}\" lint \"{target}\"")
        expect(interp_code).to_equal(0)
        step("Both lanes print the byte-identical zero-error clean verdict on stdout")
        expect(jit_out.contains("Lint passed: all files clean")).to_equal(true)
        if jit_out != interp_out:
            print "jit stdout:\n{jit_out}\ninterp stdout:\n{interp_out}"
        expect(jit_out == interp_out).to_equal(true)
